# clang-tidy configuration for the test tree.
#
# clang-tidy resolves its configuration by walking up the directory tree from
# each source file. Without this file that search leaves the repository without
# finding anything (orc/.clang-tidy covers the host tree only), so clang-tidy
# falls back to its built-in default: the whole path-sensitive
# `clang-analyzer-*` suite, which is by far the most expensive analysis it
# offers -- measured at 5-127 s per test translation unit against 3-8 s for the
# orc/ check list. The findings were never enforced either, because a fallback
# configuration carries no WarningsAsErrors, so CI paid that cost on every test
# translation unit and discarded the output.
#
# Test sources are deliberately not held to the orc/ check list: they emit
# hundreds of diagnostics under its `WarningsAsErrors: '*'`. The single check
# below is cheap, AST-only and already clean across the tree; it is present
# because clang-tidy refuses to run with no checks enabled at all.
#
# This file governs editor/clangd analysis and the repo-wide `clang-tidy-check`
# target. Per-file analysis during the build is switched off for this tree
# outright -- see the CMAKE_CXX_CLANG_TIDY reset in orc-tests/CMakeLists.txt.
Checks: '-*,modernize-use-override'
WarningsAsErrors: ''
